			<div class="content" id="post-content-2319529">
									

<p>I'mmmmmm tentatively upvoting, I suppose.</p>
<p>It's got three pretty simple narrative elements: 1) a document through which 2) an entity is screwing with the Foundation via 3) doomed neutralization ideas.</p>
<p>It's a simple narrative and most of the space is taken up by the proposals, but I think it works. (It's rare for me to enjoy someone writing hate notes to the Foundation, so that's an achievement.) Also, I think there's a good balance with the crosstesting, with you providing enough additional narrative that you aren't just riding their coat-tails.</p>
<p>The image and the lulz explanation nearly killed it for me before I got into the meat. I mean, makes sense to have an insultingly childish cover in context, but it still threw it off.</p>
<p>I have some more in-universe issues (For example, if the documents are Level 4 or higher (so O5) and they think the SCP details are accurate, who do they have reading this?), but I don't know of addressing them world help.</p>

